  <h1>DeepSeek Harness vs <span class="accent">12 coding agents</span></h1>
  <p class="muted small" style="margin-bottom:20px">August 14, 2026 · dshbase</p>

  <p>When DeepSeek V4 launched, a wave of tools rushed to run it — and the results revealed something counterintuitive: <strong>the harness you choose moves cost and capability more than the model itself</strong>. Same DeepSeek model, different tool, up to 7x cost difference. Here's the landscape, plus what we found when we actually tested the tool that's supposed to be the official answer.</p>

  <h2>The three camps</h2>
  <p>Every tool here fits one of three groups:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>General-purpose agent products</strong> — polished, tied to their own ecosystem, but not optimized for DeepSeek.</li>
    <li><strong>DeepSeek-native / cost-optimized tools</strong> — built specifically to make DeepSeek cheap and reliable.</li>
    <li><strong>DSH itself</strong> — the official, everything-is-a-plugin harness.</li>
  </ul>

